{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++11 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nThere is the faculty of Computer Science in Berland. In the social net \"TheContact!\" for each course of this faculty there is the special group whose name equals the year of university entrance of corresponding course of students at the university. Each of students joins the group of his course and joins all groups for which the year of student's university entrance differs by no more than x from the year of university entrance of this student, where x \u2014 some non-negative integer. A value x is not given, but it can be uniquely determined from the available data. Note that students don't join other groups. You are given the list of groups which the student Igor joined. According to this information you need to determine the year of Igor's university entrance.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++11 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<int> arr(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        cin >> arr[i];\n    }\n    \n    sort(arr.begin(), arr.end());\n    \n    int result = arr[1];\n    int max_min = min(arr[1] - arr[0], arr[n-1] - arr[1]);\n    \n    for (int i = 2; i < n-1; ++i) {\n        int left_gap = arr[i] - arr[0];\n        int right_gap = arr[n-1] - arr[i];\n        int min_gap = min(left_gap, right_gap);\n        if (min_gap > max_min) {\n            max_min = min_gap;\n            result = arr[i];\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << result;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<int> arr(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        cin >> arr[i];\n    }\n    \n    sort(arr.begin(), arr.end());\n    \n    // The student joins their own course group and all groups within x years\n    // So the joined groups form a contiguous range [entrance_x - x, entrance_x + x]\n    // The middle of the sorted array should be Igor's entrance year\n    // Since the range is symmetric around Igor's entrance year\n    \n    // For odd number of groups, the middle element is Igor's year\n    // For even number of groups, both middle elements are valid, but we need the lower one\n    // Actually, since the range is [entrance_x - x, entrance_x + x], the middle of the sorted array\n    // should be Igor's entrance year\n    \n    int result = arr[n/2];\n    \n    cout << result;\n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.9\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00018070495571009815, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -0.00010299152199877426, -4.529942543740617e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.1801649634435307e-05, 0.0, -5.006777428206988e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.08901623636